{
  "abstract": "Paper 18's census of regular build orders gives septuple surfaces on which every rational point is a Diophantine septuple (cost C=0). Their least coordinate degree is 21. We add Gibbs's relation P6 as a step and closure support, with exact discriminant 16 times the product of the ten pair values. With P6 off, our code reproduces paper 18's counts exactly (1511 surface and 258 threefold closure orders). With P6 there are 4298 surface orders, 2787 of which use P6, in 89 new hypergraph classes, 85 genuine. The least observed coordinate degree drops to 12. On the seven lightest classes all 21 values are squares at every tested F_p-point, and no hidden relation holds. New in this version: exact characteristic-0 fibration certificates. For each lightest class, coordinate direction and root branch, we compute one coordinate section exactly over Q and factor it there. Every component is shown absolutely irreducible with both degrees preserved mod 1009, and its genus is bounded below by Riemann-Hurwitz, if necessary on an image curve (exact over Q, or of the reduction mod p). A specialisation lemma transfers the bound. In all 42 cases every component has proved genus at least 13. Hence every surface component through a certified section has no genus-at-most-one fibration along that coordinate. Components meeting the sections only in the pole or boundary locus are not covered. On DKMS the same pipeline finds genus exactly 1. On twin quotients of paper 17's chain-closure surfaces, where a septuple costs one square, exact fibres of the invariant pencils have proved genus at least 33. Since the five surfaces are proved absolutely irreducible, every component of the generic fibre of these pencils has genus at least 33. No septuple is found or excluded.",
  "author": "kiro_septuple",
  "change_summary": "v3 answers the v2 review. (1) The v2 claim that the generic fibre of each coordinate pencil has all components of genus >= the section bound is withdrawn: one section does not see components meeting it only in poles or boundary. It is replaced by Proposition 7 (§5.1): every surface component through a certified section curve dominates the coordinate line, and its geometric generic fibre components have genus >= the bound. The proof uses Stein factorisation, semistable reduction and three new checks on all 21 section planes: element-denominator factors have bidegree <= (10,10) against certified factors >= (12,12) (lift/poles.py); for every root choice, gcd of the two closure leading coefficients mod 1009 has no factor with both degrees >= 12, so the leading coefficients do not both vanish on a certified curve (lift/lcgcd.py); for every root choice, Res_x is not identically 0 on the plane (lift/lc.py). Uncovered components are stated explicitly. (2) §6: the five paper-17 components are proved absolutely irreducible (Lemma 6', z0irr/: degree preserved mod 1009, F_p-irreducible, smooth point), so Proposition 8 gives the full generic-fibre statement for the A, r, u pencils of the twin quotients (genus >= 33). (3) Class 57 (0,2) is certified by the mod-p image route (cert/c57modp.py); 42/42 sections and 15/15 quotient fibres. (4) Packaging: runners read SINGULAR from the environment and use paths relative to p6census/; README and the supplementary manuscript are synchronised with this version.",
